WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Both my wife and I, we experienced Betsy in 1965.

2
00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:08.940
I was nineteen.

3
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:14.500
In fact, I was staying at my grandmother's house.

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:21.600
And that's when the [Army] Corps of Engineers actually did blow up the levee for Betsy.

5
00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:25.280
And it flooded the Lower Ninth Ward.

6
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:28.480
They didn't really, like I said, I guess, blow it up.

7
00:00:28.480 --> 00:00:34.260
They actually thought they could blow the levee and control the water with a barge.

8
00:00:34.260 --> 00:00:37.780
But the barge went through the levee.

9
00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:50.100
And I walked in water up to my chest and promised that if I ever had the opportunity to get out of there alive,

10
00:00:50.100 --> 00:00:53.920
I would never, ever get caught in a storm.

11
00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:57.420
And my wife and I were talking the other day.

12
00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:06.260
I guess in my forty-something years of working, we figured that we evacuated, oh, something like thirty-five times.

13
00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:12.300
Sometimes you might evacuate two or three times a season.

14
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.140
So when you say thirty-five times, it sounds like a lot.

15
00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:18.660
But if you do it every three or four times a year.

16
00:01:18.660 --> 00:01:24.100
And the reason why, because both of us got caught in Betsy.

17
00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.440
So we knew exactly what we were up against.
